    "dynamic_instructions": "{\r\n  \"datasetView\": \"**Meet the Data**\\n\\nGoal: Explore your dataset. Pick what your model will predict.\\n\\nA record is all the data about one play. In the table view, each record shows as one row.\\n\\n1. Read the **Overview** and **Data Source** below. Write the total records in **My Data** in your guide.\\n2. Click **Cards** to look through the records one at a time.\\n3. Pick one label your model will predict. Write it in My Data.\\n4. Click your label's name at the top to open Column Analysis. Write how many records have each category.\\n5. Pick two features that could help predict your label. Do step 4 for each one.\\n\\nYou are done when My Data has your label and two features, each with record counts.\\n\\nThink about: Who could use a model trained on this data?\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Overview**: \\n\\nThis dataset contains information about a variety of different football plays from the NFL.\\n\\n**Data Source**: \\n\\nnflverse play-by-play data. Each record is one real play from the 2023 NFL season\",\r\n  \"results\": \"What can you do on the **Testing** screen?\\n* Interact with your decision tree\\n* Examine the test data\\n* Trace a prediction\\n* Save your decision tree to your device or backpack\"\r\n}",
